Fixes #1989

## Summary

This PR optimizes the `add()` and `remove()` methods in `DOMTokenList` by using `Set` for O(1) token lookups instead of `Array.indexOf()` which is O(n).

## Changes

### `add()` method

**Before:**
```typescript
for (const token of tokens) {
  const index = list.indexOf(token);  // O(n) per token
  if (index === -1) {
    list.push(token);
  }
}
```

**After:**
```typescript
const existingTokens = new Set(list);
for (const token of tokens) {
  if (!existingTokens.has(token)) {   // O(1)
    existingTokens.add(token);
    list.push(token);
  }
}
```

### `remove()` method

**Before:**
```typescript
for (const token of tokens) {
  const index = list.indexOf(token);  // O(n) per token
  if (index !== -1) {
    list.splice(index, 1);            // O(n) shift
  }
}
```

**After:**
```typescript
const tokensToRemove = new Set(tokens);
const newList = list.filter((item) => !tokensToRemove.has(item));  // O(n) total
```

## Complexity improvement

| Method | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| `add()` | O(n × m) | O(n + m) |
| `remove()` | O(n × m) | O(n + m) |

Where n = existing tokens, m = tokens being added/removed.

Addresses review feedback to replace the brittle custom Zod-to-JSON-Schema implementation with the `zod-to-json-schema` library for improved robustness and maintainability.

## Changes

- **Added dependency**: `zod-to-json-schema` package
- **Removed custom converters**: Deleted `zodToJsonSchema` and `zodFieldToJsonSchema` functions (62 lines)
- **Updated tool schema generation**: `getToolSchemas()` now uses library function directly
- **Merged main branch**: Resolved merge conflicts while preserving the library-based implementation

```typescript
// Before: Custom implementation with limited Zod feature support
function zodToJsonSchema(schema: z.ZodSchema): Record<string, unknown> {
  // ... 62 lines of custom conversion logic
}

// After: Battle-tested library
import { zodToJsonSchema as convertZodToJsonSchema } from 'zod-to-json-schema';

return tools.map(tool => ({
  // ...
  parameters: convertZodToJsonSchema(tool.inputSchema) as Record<string, unknown>,
}));
```

The type assertion is necessary due to TypeScript's complex type instantiation with JsonSchema7Type.

## Merge Resolution

Successfully merged changes from main branch while maintaining the library-based approach:
- ✅ Removed unused `Product` import (aligned with main)
- ✅ Accepted async/await conversions in Firecrawl functions
- ✅ Accepted Jina base URL constants addition
- ✅ Accepted enhanced test coverage with fetch mocking
- ✅ Kept custom converter functions removed (preserving PR objective)

The custom Zod converter functions that were re-added in main have been removed again to maintain the robust library-based implementation as originally intended.

